      "observed": "The VDD power pins of both the FCC (STM32H753) and NAVC (STM32F405) MCUs are on unconnected nets, not tied to any 3.3V rail.",
      "expected": "All VDD pins should be connected to the 3.3V rail, as the specification states that 3V3 feeds both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"217\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"}
      ],
      "impact": "The MCUs receive no power and the board cannot function.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["REG2", "NAVC1", "U11", "R9", "R10", "R11", "R12", "R13", "R14", "R28", "R29", "R30", "R31"],
      "pins": ["REG2.1", "NAVC1.1", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "The LDO output (REG2.1) is on net +3.3V, while the MCU VBAT, pull-up resistors, and buffer VCC are on a separate net +3V3. There is no connection between +3.3V and +3V3.",
      "expected": "The LDO output and the MCU/sensor supply should be the same 3.3V rail, as the specification states the LDO produces 3V3 for MCUs and sensors.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") ...))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "An LD39200PU33R LDO, fed from the 5 V rail, produces 3V3 for \"MCUs and Sensors\""}
      ],
      "impact": "The +3V3 rail has no power source, so the MCUs, pull-ups, and buffer on that rail are unpowered even if their VDD pins were connected.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.7"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V"],
      "observed": "The PS (protocol select) pin of the BMI088 IMU is tied to +3.3V (logic high).",
      "expected": "For I2C operation, the PS pin must be tied low (GND). The specification states the BMI088 uses I2C addresses 0x19 and 0x69.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PS\") (pintype \"input\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "IMU (accel + gyro) | NAVCPeripherals | Bosch BMI088, I2C addr 0x19 (acc) / 0x69 (gyr)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The BMI088 is placed in SPI mode instead of I2C mode, so I2C communication with the IMU will fail and no inertial data will be available.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple severe anomalies: both MCUs have unconnected VDD pins, the 3.3V rail is split into two unconnected nets (+3.3V and +3V3), and the BMI088 IMU is configured for SPI instead of the specified I2C mode. These issues would prevent the board from powering up or functioning as intended."
}

